      "Turn-flow example: 1. Player to the dealer's left starts.\n2. ASKING: On your turn, ask a specific opponent for a specific card of a family you already hold at least one card of (e.g., 'Do you have Master Bun the Baker's Son?').\n3. RESULT: If they have it, they give it to you and you continue asking anyone for another card. If they don't have it, they say 'Not at home!' and your turn ends. The player who was asked now begins their turn.\n4. COMPLETION: When you collect all four members of a family, you must immediately lay them face-up on the table.",
      'Scoring example: Each completed family counts as one point. Player with the most points (families) wins..',
